JavaScript:

```javascript
// Get the modal and button variables
const modal = document.getElementById("modal");
const btn = document.getElementsByClassName("btn btn-primary")[0];

// Get the message inputs
const userMessageInput = document.getElementById("user-message");
const chatbotMessageInput = document.getElementById("chatbot-message");

// Set the initial values for the inputs
userMessageInput.value = "You: Hello, how are you?";
chatbotMessageInput.value = "Chatbot: Hello! I'm doing well, thank you for asking. How can I help you today?";

// Show the modal when the button is clicked
btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
  modal.style.display = "block";
});

// Clear the inputs after the modal is closed
modal.addEventListener("hidden.bs.modal", () => {
  userMessageInput.value = "";
  chatbotMessageInput.value = "";
});

// Function to add a new message to the modal
function addMessage(message) {
  const messageElement = document.createElement("p");
  messageElement.innerText = message;
  messageElement.classList.add("message");
  document.getElementById("chat-history").appendChild(messageElement);
}

// Function to add a new message from the user
function addUserMessage() {
  const message = userMessageInput.value;
  userMessageInput.value = "";
  addMessage(message);
}

// Function to add a new message from the chatbot
function addChatbotMessage() {
  const message = chatbotMessageInput.value;
  chatbotMessageInput.value = "";
  addMessage(message);
}

// Function to trigger the user message function when the user input is changed
userMessageInput.addEventListener("input", () => {
  addUserMessage();
});

// Function to trigger the chatbot message function when the chatbot input is changed
chatbotMessageInput.addEventListener("input", () => {
  addChatbotMessage();
});
```

In this example, the modal is created using HTML and is hidden by default. When the "Open modal" button is clicked, the modal is shown. When the modal is closed, the inputs are cleared so that the user can start fresh.

The `addMessage()` function is used to add a new message to the modal's chat history. The `addUserMessage()` and `addChatbotMessage()` functions are used to add a new message from the user and the chatbot, respectively. The `input` event is used to trigger these functions when the user or chatbot input is changed.

This is just a basic example, and you can customize it however you need for your specific use case.

